# SMTP Email Delivery Integration for Contact Form

This plan outlines the implementation of secure, server-side SMTP email delivery for the contact form in the portfolio website. By using Node.js (via the Angular SSR Express backend) and `nodemailer`, we keep credentials secure and avoid exposing them in client-side code.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To enable SMTP email delivery, you will need to create a `.env` file in the root of the project with your mail server details. We will provide a template `.env.example`.
> If you are using Gmail, you must generate a **Google Account App Password** rather than using your regular password. We include detailed instructions below on how to set this up.

